You should have returned directly to Jerusalem.  There is no hope for you now.	你早該直接返回耶路撒冷才是，如今已是回天乏術。
Gaza is unsafe.  Jerusalem lies somewhere beyond the desert.  Your choices are limited and filled with danger at every step.  Go with caution.	加薩並不安全。耶路撒冷就在沙漠的另一端。你的選擇不多，且步步驚險，務必謹慎而行。
You have safely left Gaza behind, but the desert lies ahead.  You will never cross it without my help.	你已安然離開加薩，但前方是茫茫沙漠。少了我的幫助，你絕無可能穿越它。
I am a man of the desert, not of the sea.	我是沙漠之子，不是海上之人。
Hire me, and I will lead you safely to water.  Trust me in all things.	雇用我，我必領你安然尋得水源。凡事都要信任我。
I urge you once more to hire me as your guide through the desert.  Only I can show you where the hidden water lies.	我再次懇請你雇我為沙漠嚮導。唯有我知曉隱藏水源的所在。
He is a useless pest.	他不過是個沒用的討厭鬼。
He is an old fraud.	他是個老騙子。
It is just an old tower.	那不過是座舊塔。
If you must ask questions, you might at least hire me as your guide.	你若非問不可，倒不如先雇我當你的嚮導。
I do not know what folly brought you back here to the hill above Gaza.  I fear you are doomed.	我不知是什麼糊塗念頭又把你帶回加薩上方這座山丘。恐怕你在劫難逃了。
From this hard-earned height above Gaza you can see far across the sea and over the village.  But ahead of you lies a searing and treacherous desert to cross.	從加薩上方這座你辛苦爬上的高地望去，能遠眺大海與村落。但橫在你前方的，是一片酷熱而險惡、必須橫越的沙漠。
I do not think you will see Hazm ever again.	我想你再也見不到哈慈了。
Undoubtedly he hurried back to his master, as instructed.	他想必已依吩咐，匆匆趕回主人身邊。
There is a slim chance he might be on the dock where you left him.	他仍有一絲可能留在你與他分別的碼頭。
Al-Sirat's enclosure is hidden somewhere in the hillside below.  You would never find it again without Hazm.	Al-Sirat 的居所就藏在下方的山坡某處。少了哈慈，你絕不可能再找到它。
You had your chance when Hazm offered to take you to the scholar.  Now it may be too late.	哈慈曾提議帶你去見那位學者，你當時本有機會。如今恐怕為時已晚。
You can barely make out the ship, let alone any other detail, from this distance.	從這個距離，你僅能勉強辨出那艘船的輪廓，更別提其他細節了。
It may be the ship you came on still in port, or another ship entirely.  It matters not.	那或許是載你來的那艘船仍泊在港中，也或許是另一艘船。這都無關緊要。
From this height above Gaza, the ship on which you spent so many weary weeks looks like a mere toy.	從加薩上方這處高地望去，那艘曾載你度過數週艱辛航程的船，看來不過像個玩具。
You saw the stone tower when you disembarked.  It looked abandoned.	你下船時曾見過那座石塔，看來已遭棄置。
The town of Gaza occupies the shoreline.	加薩城座落於這片海岸線上。
From this hard-earned height above Gaza you can see far across the sea and over the village.	從加薩上方這座你辛苦爬上的高地望去，能遠眺大海與村落。
The sea looks lovely from here.	從這裡望去，大海景色怡人。
Aye, a most impressive looking bank of clouds.	正是，那片雲堤景象著實壯觀。
You dare not look long at the glaring sun.	你不敢直視那刺目的驕陽太久。
Cross?  Ah, you refer to the mast and furled sail of the ship down at the dock.	十字？啊，你說的是碼頭那艘船上的桅杆與收捲的船帆吧。
Why do you refuse to listen to good advice?	你為何執意不聽良言？
From here you can go either into the desert or back the way you came.	從這裡，你可以走入沙漠，也可以循原路折返。
Follow me and I will lead you free of the cliffs.	跟著我，我會領你脫離這片峭壁。
In this heat, you must waste no breath upon idle chatter.	在這等酷熱之中，你可耗不起力氣閒聊。
Arthur, Arthur, why are you here?.  You should be back in Jerusalem by now.	亞瑟，亞瑟，你怎會在這裡？此刻你早該回到耶路撒冷了。
This area is enclosed by cliffs.  There are but two openings...back to the ridge overlooking Gaza or into the desert.	這片區域四面為峭壁所困，僅有兩處出口……一是回到俯瞰加薩的山脊，一是通往沙漠。
The cliffs are formidably high.	這片峭壁高聳得駭人。
This way, habib.  Follow me.	這邊走，朋友，跟著我。
Where are you going?  Follow me!	你要去哪裡？跟著我！
It is too deeply buried.	它埋得太深了。
The markings on the ancient pillar have been obliterated with the passage of time.	這根古柱上的刻痕，已被歲月磨蝕殆盡。
Your way is blocked upon one side by cliffs.  The rest upon all sides is desert.	你的一側被峭壁擋住去路，其餘各面盡是沙漠。
The high cliffs continue to one side of you.	高聳的峭壁在你一側延展而去。
It appears to be a chunk of very ancient pillar, partially buried.	看來是一截極為古老的石柱殘塊，半埋於地下。
Now that you have trudged far from the city walls, what have you to show for it?  Nothing.  You are lost in the blistering desert without water once again.	如今你已跋涉遠離城牆，可有什麼收穫？什麼也沒有。你再度迷失在這片酷熱的沙漠之中，滴水全無。
Good, you are here.  But stay close behind me or you may get lost.	好，你來了。但要緊跟在我身後，否則你會迷路的。
This way, habib.  We must go directly to the water.	這邊走，朋友，我們得直奔水源。
Beware!  Ahead of you is only vast and open desert.  This is no time to get lost.	小心！你前方只有遼闊無垠的沙漠。此刻絕不是迷路的時候。
There are rocks, barren ground and sand, and a vast array of desert stretching out in all directions, save for the way you came.	四周盡是岩石、荒地與黃沙，除了你來時的方向，沙漠向四面八方無盡延展。
There are rocks, barren ground and sand, and a vast array of desert stretching out in all directions.	四周盡是岩石、荒地與黃沙，沙漠向四面八方無盡延展。
Below you - and a lethal fall from here, I might add - is a long pool of fresh water.	你的下方——容我補一句，這一摔可是必死無疑——有一泓狹長的淡水池。
I suspect I should know what this place is.  If you investigate further it may come to me.	我猜我該認得這個地方。你若再仔細查探，或許我就能想起來。
The girl and her jug have vanished over the hill.	那女孩與她的水罐，已消失在山丘的另一頭。
If you refer to Fatima, it would seem she had a lesson to teach you.  Next time, heed her words more closely.	你若說的是法提瑪，看來她是想教你一課。下回，把她的話聽得更仔細些。
It appears dark and empty inside.	裡頭看來一片漆黑，空無一物。
Below you is an enticing pool of water.	你的下方，有一泓誘人的水池。
The platform around the pit is made of stone.	坑洞四周的平台以石塊砌成。
You are babbling, Arthur.	你在胡言亂語了，亞瑟。
He was so anxious for you to follow him, he did not wait to speak further with you.	他一心急著要你跟上，等不及再與你多說什麼。
You swallowed a great deal of water when you landed in the aqueduct.  But if you want more, now is the time to do it.	你墜入水道時已嗆下不少水。但你若還想再喝，此刻正是時候。
A fine idea, but you will not do it from up here.	好主意，但你在這上頭可辦不到。
You will have to find it, first.	你得先找到它才行。
I see nothing like that here.	此處我沒見著那樣的東西。
The dates have all been harvested from the palm.	這棵椰棗樹上的果實已被採收殆盡。
They will not soothe your thirst.  You should rather look for the source of their water.	它們解不了你的渴。你該去找的是它們水分的源頭。
The aloe is not for eating and the dates have all been harvested from the palm.	蘆薈不能吃，椰棗樹上的果實也已被採收一空。
The mule knows better than you what she should eat.	這頭騾子比你更清楚自己該吃什麼。
You no longer have your mule.	你已不再有那頭騾子了。
She has run away, Arthur.	牠跑掉了，亞瑟。
Dear me.  The heat has affected you most severely.	天哪，這酷熱已把你折騰得不輕。
You should remember the way back to Jerusalem from here.	從這裡，你應當記得回耶路撒冷的路。
There is a building and a stone platform over a deep walled pit in the ground, and steps leading down into it.	地上有一座建築與一座石砌平台，架在一口以石壁圍砌的深坑之上，並有階梯通往坑底。
There are some date palms, aloe vera and other plants nearby.	附近有幾株椰棗樹、蘆薈與其他植物。
The building appears dark and empty inside.	這座建築內部看來一片漆黑，空無一物。
It is a puzzling arch for it seems to serve no purpose.  It does not even span the pit next to it.	這座拱門令人費解，似乎毫無用處，甚至連旁邊的坑洞都跨不過去。
It is very old and appears to be no longer in use.	它十分古老，看來早已棄置不用。
The pit is lined with stone walls.	這口坑洞內壁以石塊砌成。
It is deep and walled with stone.	它既深，四壁又以石塊砌成。
Up the steep slope to the north lies Jerusalem, as you know now.	沿著北方的陡坡而上，便是耶路撒冷——這你現在已經知道了。
There is a steep slope to the north which blocks any view down here of what lies in that direction, and a large hill rises above this walled pit.	北方有一道陡坡，擋住了那個方向的視野，一座大山丘則聳立於這口石壁深坑之上。
Directly above and behind the walled pit there is a large hill.	就在這口石壁深坑的正上方與後方，有一座大山丘。
Stairs lead down to the pool.	階梯通往水池底部。
There are narrow stone stairs to the stone platform and stairs going down in one corner of the pit.	有一道狹窄的石階通往石砌平台，坑洞一角也有階梯往下延伸。
As you know, you are at the Pool of Siloam.	如你所知，你正身處西羅亞池。
It is a long, narrow pool filled with glorious, fresh water.	這是一泓狹長的水池，滿盈著清澈甘美的淡水。
The presence of plants is a hopeful sign.	植物的存在，是個令人振奮的徵兆。
The Pool in this walled pit is filled with fresh water, as good as any wadi or oasis.	這口石壁深坑中的水池滿是淡水，不遜於任何旱谷或綠洲。
She found you most frightening and wanted nothing to do with you.	她被你嚇得不輕，再也不想跟你有任何瓜葛。
There is no girl here.  You are suffering from delusions.	這裡沒有什麼女孩。你是在產生幻覺。
He has not returned.  Perhaps he waits for you elsewhere.	他還沒回來。或許他正在別處等你。
They are spirits, either good or bad, which can appear in either human or animal form.	牠們是精靈，有善有惡，能化作人形或獸形現身。
The sweet water of the Pool of Siloam has quenched your thirst for now.	西羅亞池的甘美泉水，暫時解了你的渴。
Only water will quench your burning thirst.	唯有清水，能解你那如火焚燒般的乾渴。
There are some date palms whose dates have been harvested.	這裡有幾株椰棗樹，果實已被採收。
There are some aloe vera plants and other plants that I do not know.	這裡有幾株蘆薈，還有些我不認得的植物。
There are narrow stone stairs between the stone platform and the desert.	石砌平台與沙漠之間，有一道狹窄的石階相連。
Steps lead down to an enticing pool of water.	階梯向下通往一泓誘人的水池。
Steps lead down into a deep walled pit in the ground.	階梯向下通往地面上一口石壁深坑。
There is a deep walled pit in the ground, and steps leading down into it.	地上有一口石壁深坑，並有階梯通往坑底。
You have seen enough of this tunnel for now.	這條隧道，你此刻已看得夠多了。
The tunnel is quite small and soon becomes pitch black inside.	這條隧道相當狹小，往裡走沒多久便是一片漆黑。
The water is not very deep.	這裡的水不算深。
The ground is paved with stone.	地面以石塊鋪成。
You are once more at the Pool of Siloam.  The hike back to Jerusalem awaits you.	你又再度回到了西羅亞池。回耶路撒冷的路途，還等著你去走。
The walls and ground are paved with stone.  The water flows from a tunnel carved into the rock of the hill above it.	四壁與地面皆以石塊鋪成。池水源自上方山壁鑿出的一條隧道。
Wait!  At last I know where you are.  This is the Pool of Siloam.	等等！我終於認出你身在何處了。這裡是西羅亞池。
The pool is enclosed upon four sides by stone walls.  In one wall there is a tunnel opening.	這座水池四面皆為石壁環繞，其中一面石壁上有隧道開口。
There are some aloe plants around the outside of the Pool's upper platform.	水池上方平台的外緣，長著幾株蘆薈。
There are sections of old tumbled-down wall on the platform above the Pool.	水池上方的平台上，散落著幾段傾頹的舊牆殘壁。
There is a large hill through which the aqueduct is carved.	這條水道正是穿鑿一座大山丘而成。
The tunnel is known as Hezekiah's Aqueduct.	這條隧道名為希西家水道。
I doubt your mule would have attempted those narrow stone stairs had she not been so desperate for water.	我懷疑，若非渴水渴得走投無路，你那頭騾子絕不會嘗試走上那道狹窄的石階。
There is one set of narrow stone stairs.	這裡有一道狹窄的石階。
The niche is empty.	這處壁龕空無一物。
Your mule delights in the fresh water and is ready to go on.	你的騾子暢飲清水，樂不可支，已準備好繼續上路。
It is pure and cold, flowing through the aqueduct from the Spring of Gihon.	池水純淨清冽，經水道從基訓泉流淌而來。
Your mule certainly seems to enjoy it.	你的騾子看來確實喝得暢快。
The sun burns no less fiercely overhead, though this cool pit provides some relief.	頭頂驕陽依舊灼人，不過這口陰涼的深坑倒能稍解暑氣。
Upon one side are tall cliffs.  Upon the other side, open desert.	一側是高聳的峭壁，另一側則是遼闊的沙漠。
Tall cliffs block you on one side.	高聳的峭壁擋住了你一側的去路。
Come, the water is not much farther.	來吧，水源已經不遠了。
The cliffs end and a huge, flat expanse of searing desert opens out before you.	峭壁到此為止，一片廣袤平坦、酷熱難當的沙漠在你眼前展開。
The water looks and smells most inviting.  I am surprised your mule has not drunk from it yet.	這水看來、聞來都十分誘人。你那頭騾子居然還沒喝，倒教我意外。
It is a naturally formed pool, fed by a small stream flowing down a wadi to the east.	這是一處天然形成的水池，由東邊一道旱谷流下的小溪注入。
Worry not about me, habib.  But please, you need water.  I beg you to have a drink.	別擔心我，朋友。但求求你，你需要水，懇請你喝上一口。
This is neither the time nor place.	此時此地都不合適。
You certainly could use a drink.  And the closest water is that pool.	你確實需要喝點水。而最近的水源，就是那座水池。
Nonsense.  You can barely carry what you have in this heat.	胡說。這等酷熱之下，你連身上帶的東西都快扛不住了。
Nay, I do not advise it.  They are unknown and could be dangerous.	不可，我不建議這麼做。這些東西來歷不明，可能有危險。
There is nothing but sand.	這裡除了黃沙，什麼也沒有。
You sound parched.  Wet your throat and ease your burning thirst.  Please, drink your fill.	聽你的聲音已乾渴難耐。潤潤喉，解解你這如焚的乾渴吧。請盡情暢飲。
As you see, there is water in this wadi.  Drink your fill.	如你所見，這道旱谷中有水。盡情暢飲吧。
It is a perfectly good pool.  Drink your fill.	這是一泓上好的水池。盡情暢飲吧。
